  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "RNA-only PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the strongest result so far (0.5907 accuracy, 0.5727 F1), clearly above single-profile PCA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation can improve on PCA in this best profile/aggregation setting. config_005 keeps multiprofile avgpool and changes only the RNA encoder to scvi_n200, isolating the representation effect. This is the best next step because it exploits the strongest evidence, provides a clean comparison to config_002, may directly improve validation accuracy, and informs whether a learned RNA encoder should be used before adding multimodal complexity."
